This is a classic FFmpeg "font-scaling" bug. Because your video metadata shows yuv420p(progressive), 1280x720, FFmpeg sometimes attempts to render a "fallback" version of the text if it thinks the font isn't scaling correctly to the video resolution, resulting in those smaller "ghost" lines.

Since you are on Arch, the most reliable way to kill the ghosts is to explicitly define the font file path and set the line spacing. When FFmpeg has a direct path to the .ttf file, it stops "guessing" and won't render those extra artifacts.

The "Ghost-Buster" Command
This uses the standard Arch Linux path for the DejaVu font (which is installed by default with most desktop environments).

Bash
