Chroma Ghosting: Some encoders (like those used in vMix or Church streaming software) encode metadata that tells the player to "double-scan" lines for sharpness. FFmpeg's drawtext sometimes sees this and renders the text once for the "luma" (brightness) and once for the "chroma" (color) layers. Adding format=yuv420p flattens these layers before the text is drawn.

Hardware Acceleration: If you have intel-media-driver or nvidia-utils installed on Arch, Chromium or your video player might be using hardware "enhancements" to display the text. Testing the file in a simple player like mpv (which is standard for Arch users) will tell you if the ghosting is in the file or just in the preview.

