What these flags do:
-v error: Hides all the technical "startup" text and only shows you errors (if any) and the result.

-select_streams v:0: Tells FFmpeg to look only at the first video stream (ignoring audio or subtitles).

-show_entries stream=width,height: Specifically asks for the resolution dimensions.

-of csv=p=0: Formats the output as a simple 1920,1080 or 1280,720 string, which is much easier to read than a giant block of text.

Alternative (The "Visual" Way)
If you prefer to see all the data (frame rate, codec, and bitrate) at once, you can just run:
